@page "/"

<PageTitle>lyx0z</PageTitle>

<section class="hero">
    <div class="glow glow-1"></div>
    <div class="glow glow-2"></div>

    <div class="hero-content">
        <div class="avatar">
            <img src="img/pfp.jpg" alt="lyx0z" width="180" height="180" />
        </div>

        <div class="hero-text">
            <span class="eyebrow">Software Engineer Apprentice</span>

            <h1 class="hero-title">
                <span class="gradient-text">Hi, I'm lyx0z.</span><br />
                <span>I build things in C#.</span>
            </h1>

            <p class="hero-sub">
                Apprentice software engineer with a soft spot for code that stays readable.
                Currently picking up Linux and Rust on the side. Off the clock you'll find me
                with a guitar or a bass in my hands, or somewhere in a Dota lobby.
            </p>

            <div class="hero-actions">
                <a class="btn btn-accent" href="./#projects">See my projects</a>
                <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="learning">Learn with me</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="projects">
    <div class="section-inner">
        <h2 class="section-title">Projects</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">Things I've built, from small experiments to finished pieces. More coming as I go.</p>

        <div class="project-grid">
            <a class="project" href="gameoflife">
                <div class="project-top">
                    <span class="project-icon">▦</span>
                    <span class="project-arrow">→</span>
                </div>
                <h3>Conway's Game of Life</h3>
                <p>
                    A cellular automaton running in the browser. The rules and board logic live in their own
                    project with unit tests, and the web page only renders the state and drives the animation.
                </p>
                <div class="tags">
                    <span class="tag">C#</span>
                    <span class="tag">Blazor WebAssembly</span>
                    <span class="tag">NUnit</span>
                </div>
            </a>

            <a class="project" href="https://github.com/lyx0z/Notepad" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                <div class="project-top">
                    <span class="project-icon">✎</span>
                    <span class="project-arrow">↗</span>
                </div>
                <h3>Notepad</h3>
                <p>
                    A text editor in C#. File handling sits in its own FileUtils project, which was my first
                    real attempt at keeping logic out of the app that consumes it.
                </p>
                <div class="tags">
                    <span class="tag">C#</span>
                    <span class="tag">File IO</span>
                    <span class="tag">Multi project solution</span>
                </div>
            </a>
        </div>

        <a class="learn-banner" href="learning">
            <div>
                <h3>Learn with me</h3>
                <p>Every exercise repo from C# basics through collections, plus where I am with Rust.</p>
            </div>
            <span class="project-arrow">→</span>
        </a>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="about">
    <div class="section-inner">
        <h2 class="section-title">About me</h2>

        <div class="about-grid">
            <p class="about-text">
                I'm a software engineering apprentice. C# is where I'm most at home and most of what I build
                starts there. Right now I'm learning Linux and Rust to get a better feel for what actually happens
                underneath the frameworks. I care about code that still makes sense six months later: small classes,
                clear names, and logic kept apart from the UI that shows it.
            </p>

            <div class="about-cards">
                <div class="card">
                    <h3>Comfortable with</h3>
                    <div class="tags">
                        <span class="tag tag-strong">C#</span>
                        <span class="tag tag-strong">.NET</span>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="card">
                    <h3>Learning right now</h3>
                    <div class="tags">
                        <span class="tag">Blazor</span>
                        <span class="tag">Linux</span>
                        <span class="tag">Rust</span>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="card">
                    <h3>Away from the keyboard</h3>
                    <div class="tags">
                        <span class="tag">Guitar</span>
                        <span class="tag">Bass</span>
                        <span class="tag">Dota</span>
                        <span class="tag">Warcraft</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
